    "bio": "Yashasvi Jaiswal is an Indian international cricketer born on December 28, 2001, in Suriyawan, Uttar Pradesh. He overcame a challenging childhood, moving to Mumbai at a young age to pursue cricket, where he lived in a tent and sold street food. Jaiswal made his Test debut for India on July 12, 2023, against West Indies, scoring an impressive 171 runs. Known for his aggressive left-handed opening batting style, he quickly established himself in the Test arena, notably scoring two consecutive double centuries against England in early 2024."
